    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Each client's page now has a Contacts section that lists that client's contacts (name, email, role) and has a form to add a new one. Both Playwright tests pass under `bin/e2e`: one checks the list shows only that client's contacts, the other adds a contact.\n\nOne thing to know: the request mentioned an OfficeFloor server, but this app is a plain Spring Boot app (only the Java package is named `net.officefloor`). I followed the Spring conventions in `CLAUDE.md`.\n\n**Database:** `V8__create_contact.sql` creates a `contact` table linked to `client`, with an index on the client and the same email-format check the client table uses.\n\n**Server:** a new `contact` package with the usual entity, repository, service and controller. It adds two endpoints:\n- `GET /api/clients/{clientId}/contacts` lists a client's contacts.\n- `POST /api/clients/{clientId}/contacts` adds one.\n\nAn unknown client returns 404. Name, email and role are all required, and email uses the same rule as clients. To share that rule I made `ClientRequest.EMAIL_PATTERN` public. The test-only reset and seed endpoints now clear and load contacts too.\n\n**Front end:** a new `ClientContacts` component in `features/contacts/`, built the same way as the existing client-projects section, sits between the client's details and its projects. It has an add form with field-level errors and shows messages when the list is empty or fails to load. It uses all the `data-testid` values the spec expects, plus a few more for the email column, the errors and the empty state. No existing `data-testid` was renamed or removed.\n\nThe spec doesn't expect any audit record, so adding a contact writes nothing to the audit log.",
